    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how number puzzles become equations.\n\nThe book's main idea is simple: choose the unknown number, turn each condition into math, solve, and check.\n\nWe will begin with one unknown before moving to harder number puzzles.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Start by giving the unknown number a simple name, usually x.\n\nThen translate the sentence, not the answer.\n\nExample: 'x is as much greater than 28 as it is less than 64' means\n\nx − 28 = 64 − x.\n\nBoth sides describe the two gaps.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
